    "done_when": "A driver run on the fleet compute node this session already holds, using imas_ambix.data.eddb.fetch_channels and the merged extractor with no new repository module, writes into JT60SA_ROOT: (a) on E101154, the first-pass channels MMSYS cur{CS1..CS4,EF1..EF6}{HiTe,LKAT}, cur1TFLKAT, cur2TFLKAT; PSRC Ip, calIp, magFluxLp1..34, magPbTC1..23; MDAC curAVVRC1..4; (b) on E101154 and on E101173, every MDAC data name EDDB's catalogue lists for that shot that begins magFlxLp, with the names enumerated from the catalogue rather than assumed. Each shot's fetch is one ssh session through fetch_channels, which skips channels already cached (E101173's first pass is). A warm re-read of every channel fetched in this run through VirtualZarrView, with a transport that raises if called, makes no transport call. The evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-eddb-second-cold-fetch.html records per shot: channels requested, served and refused, each refusal with the irc fetch_channels returned; cold wall time and per-signal wall time; bytes on disk; unit strings; the time-base length of each served channel; and the full list of MDAC data names beginning mag that the catalogue lists for each shot, with their counts, as names only. It states which of PSRC magFluxLp1..34 and MDAC magFlxLp* are served on each shot. No EDDB value is committed to the repository. Every ssh call uses the extractor's DEFAULT_SSH_COMMAND, which carries -F /home/ITER/mcintos/.ssh/config, and every remote command runs under nice -n 19.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "measure a cold EDDB fetch of E101154's first-pass channels and the raw MDAC flux loops on E101154 and E101173",
